# Workflow State File Format

**File**: `{{workflow.file}}`

## YAML format

Use strictly valid YAML with lowercase keys. Optional lines may be omitted.

```yaml
phase: <current-phase>
issue: <optional-dash-delimited-current-work-phrase>
plan: <optional-plan-document-path>
tracking: <optional-external-tracker-reference>
description: <optional-description>
queue:
  - <optional-queued-issue-id>
```

`phase` is required. `issue` is a dash-delimited current-work phrase with no
spaces and only filesystem-friendly characters; `plan` is a relative path to an
existing plan document.{{#openspec}} Include an OpenSpec change
identifier in `issue` for an active change.{{/openspec}} Use `tracking` only for
an external issue-tracker reference, such as a Linear identifier; it is a
single string, not a mapping. Omit `tracking` when no external issue is
associated, and omit `queue` when it is empty.

## Instructions

- Read the exact configured path `{{workflow.file}}` directly; never discover it through a glob, repository search, or tracked-file listing.
- Update `{{workflow.file}}` whenever workflow state changes.
- Use the `send_file_content` MCP tool to send the complete file content after every update.
